### POST /v1/auth/login — issue a session token
###
### When to use: whenever you need a JWT to call protected endpoints
### (matchmaking-api). In dev, the login auto-provisions the player — there is
### no separate registration endpoint.
###
### How to use:
###   1. Start auth-service:
###      mvn -pl services/auth-service exec:java -Dexec.mainClass=com.victor.matchmaking.auth.AuthServiceApplication
###   2. Run the "happy path" request below.
###   3. The response token is captured into the `token` client variable,
###      used by the matchmaking-api requests.
###
### Expected: 200 with { "token": "...", "expiresIn": 3600 }.
### Error case: missing/blank playerId returns 400.

@authBaseUrl = http://localhost:8081

### Happy path — expect 200
POST {{authBaseUrl}}/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "playerId": "player-1"
}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.token); %}

### Error case — expect 400
POST {{authBaseUrl}}/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{}
